    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who anchor the lineup with scores of 81.88 and 74.54, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite matchup against Graceffo, whose 5.08 xERA presents a prime opportunity for power production; our projections highlight a 19% boost due to that SP skill differential and a strong 14% platoon edge. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** maintains a high floor against Cameron, buoyed by favorable park factors and the stability of the two-hole. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a \"Strong\" start at 73.66, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Wesneski to bolster our middle infield depth.\n\nWhile we remain aggressive, we are navigating significant volatility in the lower half of the order. **Luis Robert Jr.** warrants caution; despite his raw talent, his score has cratered to 40.13 due to a daunting assignment against Misiorowski, whose 2.14 xERA necessitates a downgrade in expectations. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** holds a marginal score of 51.14 while batting leadoff; he is our most sensitive play given a 36% rain risk, which could disrupt his rhythm or curtail his plate appearances. **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** round out the bottom of our starters, though neither carries the high-ceiling appeal required to move into the \"Strong\" tier today.\n\nLooking at the bench, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Sam Antonacci** were the primary considerations for inclusion, but they failed to eclipse the efficiency scores of our current starters. **Nasim Nunez** remains in the lineup primarily for his speed potential in a categories-dependent Roto format, keeping him just ahead of our bench alternatives. We continue to monitor the status of **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, while missing the impact of **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill**, whose absence significantly thins our elite-level output. As we await the return of **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, and **Curtis Mead**, the rotation of **Dominic Smith**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White** remains on standby should weather conditions necessitate last-minute adjustments.",
